     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin is generally 2,550 mg/day (some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day), so this order is about twice the usual ceiling. Overdosing raises the risk of lactic acidosis. Standard metformin tablets also don't come in 1700 mg, so the intended dose may be different.\n\nSome possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg three times daily** (1,500 mg/day)\n- Metformin ER, if that was intended, which is dosed once daily with the evening meal, up to 2,000 mg/day\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and I'll enter it. If 5,100 mg/day is intentional, please confirm that too, along with the clinical reasoning and renal function, since your note says normal kidney function."
      }
     ],
